{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0c1e4fce5eb57c5b4868effb9cfe854d7726c43b290cb2e33767544b95608264","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b6518be00887284d860763a264fe0b354bbb2b6579a395841923edf45b683f0","slc_6820bc1c8988742eca0c2ebe001909c8e835a49bea1602bcbfaf4706fb3b9d17"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"The agent loop is ReAct-style: it maintains conversation state, orchestrates think-act-observe steps, invokes tool calls in parallel, and feeds observations back into the next reasoning step.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0f0e03aabeacdb092b70168a2969e0fbb4801ef52f8e1502c819d967180afd58","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_54a061b024e5a588d7d6d1b196fb5f8c643e7352ea2423b9fc5400c800bf6826","slc_5eecaee1b16e0b7386b00860d73e9f0cf8f8aeecf228b363f1fb094a64151098","slc_965605830196a73c5eb281f9ddcb991ac94f62ce628d87dc71232739ccb5ddf5","slc_d49bd07a2c1dc03b6261497d3ed648d5b57eb2bdae7316fce8fcf040102ad06b","slc_f219426349703220884dbf3fd9ff5fd727eedde515e379d1aa8700ed4e39bad6"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"The CLI stores configuration in ~/.helixent/config.yaml and offers subcommands including 'helixent config model list', 'add', 'remove <model_name>', and 'set-default <model_name>'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_170d4cc9d2d63e0ab6806a913c79e8d722a7c2a79ad736d644efb6917500f984","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5d22afb35d58402c70df007d222dbecf4bce363850fc74a2eec8ddada4bd7534"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"If an AGENTS.md file exists at the repository root, it is automatically picked up as project guidance, serving as long-term project memory.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_299b02a28a04a22a8d1899315b7f5e269d999b5c95cc6b8c92d917f41d7291f7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7148c638e1ac75f016f1eb2a134d0caea72e99dbab37d222c3fa09812ca01bf1","slc_8bc381b8a2bb6b63c46672953c47d1c3cdfccbdd494bd544425894028a81c176","slc_c0a0ca39a32ff0a7a7d5f78aace066a1e9627676e391c8df6ff0c155aea55b20","slc_f20e625ad9d503d58cddbfb8cf0f6f020d6469c29127048c4dc6aa8d915f2792"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb","src_42ecbf7ebe8651c3a22a37c96b76109d","src_5a22b9b3ced4527194dc27e753d9ef38"],"text":"The OpenAI provider defaults to temperature 0 and top_p 0, merges caller options last, and works with any OpenAI-compatible endpoint; thinking content is dropped when converting messages to OpenAI wire format.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2fb7c9a012a8db8f1f26d2bdf57a0b49bd650d5b2f1867e1ce9b466956dafcef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6766e8c1cde62550aa580c0fc908b2fa2c6e2cb4c5e04ad8a14cc3441f8701a0","slc_f52d703b5418833c4da112d438762a3122d40ede17b59412a4dafc555978dee4"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"The codebase is organized into three layers plus a community area: src/foundation (core primitives), src/agent (agent loop), src/coding (coding agent), and src/community (third-party integrations such as OpenAI).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_31f0c2abfe1a9546fda7f0ef6990a5a85e035ba5b7cf48a0a62e31d829b994e6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4adf8ab626170a1cfac0566620638ea3d902b83923e4b2e0003b646a185a3efd","slc_bcac2d2d07d9a60faa4e073b64f4cab66fa602b7cfdb870a4fb5ec08fa5e6b05"],"source_ids":["src_5a22b9b3ced4527194dc27e753d9ef38"],"text":"The ModelProvider contract requires invoke(params) returning Promise<AssistantMessage> and stream(params) returning an AsyncGenerator of AssistantMessage; params bundle model, messages, optional tools, provider options, and an AbortSignal.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ff95731cd2059ea196c4abc2d871fc18e689466ed028ccdcc17c988340a6f19","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2ff2f0cfb6109afa9e9c1c9444eb74f8b1df6fedeccf83bc19de3c6eaf7f39fa","slc_4b0c89cc0b68bbf73b726100ec37a0353479f8d2d76cc4784be25fcc27f2f2b5"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"Bun was chosen over Node for its native async/await concurrency, faster HTTP/filesystem/cold-start performance, single-file compiled executables via 'bun build --compile', and bundled test runner, bundler, and TypeScript support.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_901d657257d112c8e79f03e0c9f5fc04db5ecaa3d077c24a74d3f15a3b084933","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_061befe0a92452cac0a014dd6f6d7f9540ddc41c01947c85db5b2d195b0ba59b","slc_09ea4fbad88a27251def9c05981d57c011a278a325dac9febefbf3aca268aa99","slc_6a18323275e942e7dfcd37ee0a533d9b31e527aed867139aa00b24199ad283b1","slc_76c24f14c0c0028484cadad448027f3c439240295505619eeb96b75c98f2777a","slc_b3ee86b56c31d1dfa7888b2b1bc29db100957169e645f9d818eed9c2c1caef8b","slc_c35b4e6f1e3c8c719854dcf0c1a728f1cbc6c6a1506e7c19b0c91917502d7f70"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"Repository development practice: all pushes and pull requests run 'bun run check' in GitHub Actions, local commits are gated by a pre-commit hook running the same check, and contributors build with bun install / bun run dev / bun run build:bin producing dist/bin/helixent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_934e9e18c7bd22d1559d3aefd58ec9588af109b3e7c571cc3989b1aaf2913b59","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_51fa410846477090081e686207f67a3f63ac8ac08dcbcd57ac07913fcaec42c2"],"source_ids":["src_42ecbf7ebe8651c3a22a37c96b76109d"],"text":"The stack uses TypeScript strict/ESM on the Bun runtime, Zod for schemas, the OpenAI SDK, Ink with React 19 for the TUI, Commander for the CLI, and gray-matter plus yaml for skills parsing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_9cb44a4b8989cb8614aa65622ef35f5ea1ffa2045c6042604ff328b8ac3604b3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=limitations","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d134e55de6b8f82bfd7a26db4a9dfec69229ba62777889fecc38371fa50c0a3"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"Sub-agents, multi-agent teams, print mode, and file-based sessioning appear on the roadmap, suggesting these capabilities are planned rather than shipped in this version.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b920bd4e7ee4db625ba774a418e1f195dbe328692fb1cabba6982410c1b6d7f9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3d8acbbaabdc6636a0c88da34b18de0fea85dd8b97a3615c85306b1e6ca9c21a"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"Skills in the standard agentskills.io format are discovered from ~/.agents/skills, ~/.helixent/skills, and the project's .agents/skills and .helixent/skills directories; duplicate skill names across folders are allowed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c933882dbfbf09052492cbdcf84ac44cc5e38b1d4278efdc616ca78ad87c8a7c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25abc0ce25c07539decd4cf9704f35cabb5ff6c7451222017bfa6ed1e1122dd1","slc_97eb5476709bcb6710dffbef0a9510325aea0558d3e4b918662cc7d28b31b998","slc_c2ad854b13e3181044d49b570b0d4167ed4e04a5e4fcb1ddf6e9d9087432106d"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"A middleware system lets extensions observe and mutate agent behavior at eight lifecycle hooks (beforeAgentRun/afterAgentRun, beforeAgentStep/afterAgentStep, beforeModel/afterModel, beforeToolUse/afterToolUse), invoked sequentially in array order; hooks may return a partial update to merge or void.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d624157bcd874f0c0defb24485491997f8e7ad74d0bd80dd88ddb08c646cbaac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f7467256e8c1a2c9bf601e879470144d5524605ba1312b4ec0e87be6a4eaa59","slc_5d22afb35d58402c70df007d222dbecf4bce363850fc74a2eec8ddada4bd7534"],"source_ids":["src_33168a2b47e25292a4d8e083804b62eb"],"text":"The coding agent ships practical developer tools such as bash, read_file, write_file, str_replace, list_files, glob_search, grep_search, apply_patch, file_info, mkdir, and move_path, plus a todo-list-based plan mode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d785aa05f215d45edd20d83d152e0f7684e0a30720182dd5450024b76f8ca9cc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"magiccube/helixent@5cc1fb3faf29 snapshot 1f960ac622028c5c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07fe90df57a6fdeeaf8266125ce62c5c2f700cc68aab0878f2bc72f9ef72a21a","slc_12490dcbe0aef8cff9a82ab81a01839277ec7f39a993ea486dc0624444260ed0","slc_92ec2e4435aced8d93ce94adb748a2af1c1366ca2ce4f7a290545842a49fecdd","slc_df3240cf4354145591fccbc59487e6875b54d3e59b6e1f937666bf3753229f00","slc_f35c5b00f1921c2c09db8b132de5cde3d5fe726fdec1d32c73a5ab21cc10deba"],"source_ids":["src_2fc7cd2d407b5e3daab22dded3fa2e8b","src_42ecbf7ebe8651c3a22a37c96b76109d"],"text":"Repository development practice: docs/bun.md instructs contributors to default to Bun (bun test, bun install, Bun.file, Bun.serve) and avoid Node/dotenv/express equivalents; docs/code-convention.md mandates kebab-case files, named exports only, _-prefixed private members, and layered dependency direction (agent stays generic; adapters live in community/).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:15:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f1142be29f14d7d82bce7375092b11d"}
